# Miracle Touch Salon — UX/UI Audit Report

> [!NOTE]
> This comprehensive 7-phase audit covers visual hierarchy, component consistency, core booking flows, accessibility, responsiveness, microcopy, and performance based on the current Next.js (Tailwind v4) implementation of the Miracle Touch Salon app.

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 1 — VISUAL INVENTORY
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**Overview**: The design language establishes a premium, luxury aesthetic using high contrast (`#000000` backgrounds with `#c9a84c` Gold accents) and a sharp typographic blend of Modern Sans (`Futura`/`Poppins`) and elegant Serif (`Playfair Display`/`Cormorant`/`IM Fell English`). 

ISSUE: Inconsistent Font Pairings Across Headers
PHASE: 1
SEVERITY: Medium
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/` (About, Experience vs. Services)
PROBLEM: While most headings use `font-playfair`, `About.tsx` uses `font-playfair` for the main title but switches abruptly to `font-cormorant` for the "Opening hours" card. `Team.tsx` uses `font-poppins` for cards while `Testimonials.tsx` recently upgraded to `font-futura` and `font-im-fell`. This inconsistency dilutes the unified premium brand feel.
FIX: Standardize header scales. Use `font-playfair` for all primary section headers and `font-futura` for all secondary UI text/cards. Reserve `font-im-fell` solely for quotes.
EFFORT: S

ISSUE: Floating Action Buttons Color Clash
PHASE: 1
SEVERITY: Low
LOCATION: `src/components/layout/FloatingActions.tsx`
PROBLEM: The vivid green (`#25D366`) WhatsApp icon clashes harshly against the vintage luxury gold (`#c9a84c`) and `mint` (`#9bffa3`) aesthetic of the site.
FIX: Wrap the WhatsApp icon in a monochrome or dark glassmorphic pill (similar to the Phone number) and only show the native green on `hover`.
EFFORT: XS

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 2 — COMPONENT AUDIT
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ISSUE: Redundant Button/Link Implementations
PHASE: 2
SEVERITY: Medium
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/Services.tsx` vs `Team.tsx` vs `Testimonials.tsx`
PROBLEM: Action buttons are not abstracted into a reusable UI component. `Services.tsx` hardcodes the "Explore all Services" button classes, `Testimonials.tsx` hardcodes "Experience The Excellence", and `FloatingActions.tsx` hardcodes "Book Now". This leads to slight variations in padding, hover transitions, and tracking.
FIX: Create a `<Button variant="primary" | "secondary" />` component in `src/components/ui/Button.tsx`. Consume this unified button globally.
EFFORT: M

ISSUE: Form Inputs Lack Accessible Wrappers
PHASE: 2
SEVERITY: High
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/BookingSection.tsx`
PROBLEM: The booking inputs are styled inline with `border-b` but lack explicit `:focus-visible` ring parameters or `aria-required` tags. Screen reader compatibility for dropdowns (e.g., Service selection) is minimal.
FIX: Implement Radix UI primitives or standard accessible wrappers for standard inputs, ensuring focus states have a high-contrast offset ring (not just a border color change).
EFFORT: M

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 3 — USER FLOW ANALYSIS
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

**Focus Flow**: Booking an Appointment (`/book` & `BookingSection.tsx`)

ISSUE: Booking Form is a "Dead End" State
PHASE: 3
SEVERITY: Critical
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/BookingSection.tsx`
PROBLEM: The form has an `onSubmit={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); }}` placeholder. When users spend time typing their details and hit "Book Appointment", absolutely nothing happens—no optimistic loading state, no success toast, no API connection. This causes high friction and user abandonment.
FIX: Wire the form to a server action or API route (e.g., Resend to send an email, or Twilio for SMS). Add a `isSubmitting` state that turns the button into a loading spinner, followed by a `<SuccessModal />` upon completion.
EFFORT: L

ISSUE: No direct path from "Team/Stylist" to "Book Stylist"
PHASE: 3
SEVERITY: Low
LOCATION: `src/app/blog/page.tsx` & `Team.tsx`
PROBLEM: Users browsing the stylist profiles/socials or the Before/After gallery cannot seamlessly book *that specific service*.
FIX: Pass URL query parameters when clicking "Book" under a specific service (e.g. `href="/contact?service=hair-fixing"`), and read those parameters in the `BookingSection` to auto-populate the `<select>` dropdown.
EFFORT: S

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 4 — ACCESSIBILITY (WCAG 2.1 AA)
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ISSUE: Low Contrast on Muted/Gray Text
PHASE: 4
SEVERITY: High
LOCATION: `src/app/globals.css` and `BookingSection.tsx`
PROBLEM: The `--color-salon-muted` (`#8e8e8e`) text used against the pitch-black `#000000` background barely passes WCAG AA for small text, and the placeholder text in the Booking `textarea` (`placeholder:text-gray-500`) fails contrast requirements entirely.
FIX: Lighten the placeholder text to `#a4a3a3` and explicitly define typography opacities (e.g. `text-white/70`) that guarantee 4.5:1 contrast against black.
EFFORT: XS

ISSUE: Hover Triggers on Touch Devices
PHASE: 4
SEVERITY: Medium
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/Team.tsx`
PROBLEM: The Instagram image overlays (`group-hover:opacity-100`) contain the captions and likes. On mobile (touch devices), hover states do not trigger reliably, making this content inaccessible to touch users.
FIX: Add a CSS media query `@media (hover: none)` forcing the opacity to be semi-visible natively on mobile, or reveal caption on immediate tap.
EFFORT: S

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 5 — RESPONSIVE & MOBILE AUDIT
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ISSUE: Floating Actions Blocking Footer Content
PHASE: 5
SEVERITY: Medium
LOCATION: `src/components/layout/FloatingActions.tsx` / `Mobile 375px`
PROBLEM: The global Floating Actions widget on the bottom right rests cleanly, but on highly compressed mobile layouts (e.g., iPhone SE/320px), the Book Now text and WhatsApp dual-pill take up ~50% of the screen width, potentially overlapping core `Footer.tsx` links when scrolled to the bottom.
FIX: Consolidate the widget on mobile devices into a single circular FAB (Floating Action Button) that expands into a mini-menu upon touch, ensuring 100% thumb reachability while saving screen real estate.
EFFORT: M

ISSUE: Scroll Snap Misalignment in Testimonials
PHASE: 5
SEVERITY: Low
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/Testimonials.tsx`
PROBLEM: The horizontal row of testimonials uses `snap-mandatory snap-x` with fixed `w-[365px]` cards. On 320px screen widths, the 365px card overflows the maximum viewport width, breaking horizontal snapping alignment.
FIX: Change card width to `w-[85vw] md:w-[365px]` to ensure it comfortably fits inside any mobile viewport while maintaining alignment.
EFFORT: XS

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 6 — CONTENT & MICROCOPY REVIEW
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ISSUE: Over-generic Action Labels
PHASE: 6
SEVERITY: Low
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/Pricing.tsx` & `Services.tsx`
PROBLEM: The label "Explore all Services" is used repeatedly. The CTA in the hero says "Book a consultation", while the booking section button says "Book Appointment". This mixes intents (Consultation vs Appointment).
FIX: Unify the primary conversion action terminology. Since services are premium, use "Reserve a Consultation" globally for booking actions to maintain a high-end, consultative tone.
EFFORT: XS

ISSUE: Missing Empty States for API Calls
PHASE: 6
SEVERITY: Medium
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/Testimonials.tsx`
PROBLEM: Current logic `const reviews = data?.reviews ?? [];` handles empty reviews silently. If the Google Reviews API fails or is empty, the user sees an empty black box or a weird layout gap.
FIX: Introduce a fallback static array of curated testimonials if `reviews.length === 0`, ensuring the section always looks populated.
EFFORT: S

---

## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## PHASE 7 — PERFORMANCE & INTERACTION QUALITY
## ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

ISSUE: LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) Delayed by Hero Image
PHASE: 7
SEVERITY: High
LOCATION: `src/components/sections/Hero.tsx`
PROBLEM: While the `Hero.tsx` correctly uses the `priority` flag on `currentIndex === 0`, the heavy asset `hero-banner.png` (1.7MB) and `hero-banner-mobile-view.png` (500KB) causes a massive spike in LCP. 
FIX: Convert all hero `.png` and `.jpg` banner assets to `.webp` format natively. Implement `blurDataURL` to show an immediate skeleton/blurred placeholder while the high-res desktop hero mounts.
EFFORT: M

ISSUE: CLS on Font Load 
PHASE: 7
SEVERITY: Medium
LOCATION: `src/app/layout.tsx`
PROBLEM: The app imports 6 explicit Google Fonts (`Playfair`, `Cormorant`, `Poppins`, `Syne`, `IM Fell`, `Wittgenstein`). High payload causes layout shifts when swapping from native fonts to web fonts.
FIX: Prune unused fonts. Given the recent UI updates, `Syne` and `Cormorant` appear heavily redundant. Consolidate to `Playfair`, `Futura` (local), and `Poppins` to drastically reduce render-blocking times. 
EFFORT: M

